  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\n- Generic method setups and verifications match on every type argument (#417, closes #413). A type argument that no parameter or return type uses was ignored, so a Name<string>() setup also answered Name<int>(), and a Tag<int>(1) call counted toward verifying Tag<string>(1). Each type argument now has to match.\n\n  Behaviour change: such a type argument now has to be the same type, not just a compatible one. A Name<object>() setup no longer answers Name<string>(). Set up each instantiation you call, or use a type argument the call actually uses.\n\nPerformance\n\n- Imposters create their property, event and indexer collections on first use (#418, closes #404). Constructing an imposter no longer allocates storage for members that are never set up, called or verified.\n- Arg<T>.Is(value), IsNot(value) and the implicit conversion allocate only the matcher (#420, closes #399). They no longer allocate a closure and a delegate as well. Arg<T>.Is(predicate) grows from 24 to 40 bytes as a trade-off.",
